OL,3,GNEWSAFishermen seek urgent help with
OL,4,Asoaring fuel costs
OL,5,
OL,6,FFishermen say they will be forced out
OL,7,Fof business unless the government
OL,8,Fsubsidises the cost of their fuel.
OL,10,FThey are calling on ministers to follow
OL,11,Fthe EU's lead and provide help to an
OL,12,Findustry "vital to UK food security".
OL,14,FPaul Trebilcock, of fish supplier W
OL,15,FStevens and Sons, said the government
OL,16,Fallowed subsidised EU fleets access to
OL,17,FUK waters while local fishermen
OL,18,Freceived no help. "The EU gives 20p of
OL,19,Fsubsidy per litre to their fleets but
OL,20,Four government does nothing - it
OL,21,Fbeggars belief."
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,345,340,200,160,0,100
